SUMMARY:Evidence informed policy and policy informed research for cleaner a
 ir
LOCATION:Chemistry Dept\, Unilever Lecture Theatre and Teams
URL:https://talks.cam.ac.uk/talk/index/273542/
CATEGORIES:Policy
DESCRIPTION:Speaker: Dr Sarah Moller\nCentre for Atmospheric Science semina
 rs\, Chemistry Dept.\nTopics: Policy\nDetails: https://talks.cam.ac.uk/tal
 k/index/273542/\nAir pollution is the greatest environmental risk to human
  health\, affecting almost every system in the body and at every stage of 
 life. It also damages ecosystems and leads to biodiversity loss. Science h
 as played a central role in demonstrating the need for action and in devel
 oping air quality standards and policies to deliver progress. In the UK th
 ere are well-established mechanisms for providing science advice for polic
 y\, including Chief Scientific Advisers in each government department\, an
 d a network of science advisory councils and expert groups. \n\n I have wo
 rked at the science policy interface for the past 14 years. Through the in
 sights provided from bridging the academic and policy communities I have f
 acilitated a transformation in how the Defra air pollution team approaches
  interactions with both the research community and research funders\, resu
 lting in better access to and uptak
END:VEVENT
