 k\, Professor Angie Hobbs explores how Plato can help us with these urgent
  questions\, and how he addresses the key issue of character formation\, a
 nd why it never benefits us to return wrong for wrong. She shows how she h
 as used his methodology\, ideas and arguments in a variety of sectors to a
 ddress contemporary issues in education\, faith–secular debate\, health 
 care and the civil service\, and invites the audience to discuss with
END:VEVENT
