 e of attribution research quantified climate change impacts on the intensi
 ty and probability of extreme weather events and slow-onset changes in gla
 ciers and sea levels. Over the past decade\, impact attribution studies ha
 ve extended these methods to assess the attributable impacts of extreme ev
 ents on agriculture\, health\, economic losses and biodiversity. Concurren
 tly\, source attribution research quantified individual emitters’ contri
 butions to climate change impacts.\n Steady progress towards 
