UID:dept-www-law-cam-ac-uk-press-events-2026-12-lunchtime-conversation-what
 -special-@cambridge-events
DTSTAMP:20261118T073026Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20261204T130000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20261204T140000
SUMMARY:LCIL lunchtime conversation: 'What is Special about the Special Tri
 bunal for the Crime of Aggression against Ukraine?'
LOCATION:Lauterpacht Centre for International Law
URL:https://www.law.cam.ac.uk/press/events/2026/12/lunchtime-conversation-w
 hat-special-about-special-tribunal-crime-aggression-against-ukraine
CATEGORIES:Law,International,Criminology
DESCRIPTION:Faculty of Law\nTopics: Law\, International\, Criminology\nDeta
 ils: https://www.law.cam.ac.uk/press/events/2026/12/lunchtime-conversation
 -what-special-about-special-tribunal-crime-aggression-against-ukraine\nDat
 e/time: \n\n Friday 4 December 2026 \n\n 1:00pm to 2:00pm\n\n Location: \n
 \n Lauterpacht Centre for International Law\n\n Berkowitz/Finley Lecture H
 all\n\n About \n\n Register here if attending online   At a time when som
 e international courts and tribunals are under attack\, defunded or otherw
 ise obstructed\, a new one is being created: the Special Tribunal for the 
 Crime of Aggression against Ukraine. Ukrainian legal scholar Dr Gaiane Nur
 idzhanian \, in conversation with LCIL Fellow Professor Sarah Nouwen\, wil
 l explore what is special about the tribunal: why is it needed\, what is i
 ts legal nature\, what are its prospects and the role in the development o
 f international law? \n There is a sandwich lunch at 12.30 pm in the Old 
 Library at the Centre. All lecture attendees welcome.\n The Friday Lunchti
 me Lecture series is kindly supported by Cambridge University Press & Asse
 ssment .
END:VEVENT
